        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(config): reject zero-value resetArchiveRetention to prevent silent data loss",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nConfiguring `session.maintenance.resetArchiveRetention: \"0h\"` (or any string that `parseDurationMs` evaluates to zero) is silently accepted by Zod config validation. `parseDurationMs(\"0h\")` returns `0` without throwing, so the `superRefine` passes the value. `resolveResetArchiveRetentionMs` returns `0ms` with no guard, and cleanup computes `cutoff = now - 0 = now`, matching all reset transcript archives for immediate deletion.\n\n## Changes\n\n**Schema gate (prevention)**: Added `ms <= 0` guard in `superRefine` to reject any string that `parseDurationMs` evaluates to ≤ 0 at config validation time. The documented disable sentinel (`false`) is unaffected.\n\n**Doctor migration (upgrade safety)**: Added a registered legacy rule + migration in the existing session maintenance migration file that uses `parseDurationMs` (same `{ defaultUnit: \"d\" }` options as schema) in both detection and repair paths. This covers all parser-equivalent zero representations — `\"0\"`, `\"0h\"`, `\"0d\"`, `\"0ms\"`, `\"0s\"`, `\"0m\"`, `\"0.0h\"`, `\"0h0m\"`, `\"0h0m0s\"`, etc. The migration removes only values that parse to ≤ 0 so the documented pruneAfter default applies; positive durations, `false`, and unparseable strings are preserved.\n\n### Files changed (4 files, +248/-3)\n\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `src/config/zod-schema.session.ts` | +14/-3: reject zero-duration in superRefine |\n| `src/config/zod-schema.session-maintenance-extensions.test.ts` | +27: schema regression cases |\n| `src/commands/doctor/shared/legacy-config-migrations.runtime.session.ts` | +49: parser-backed rule + migration spec |\n| `src/commands/doctor/shared/legacy-config-migrations.runtime.session.test.ts` | +155: 16 focused tests |\n\n## Evidence\n\n### All tests passing\n\n```\n$ node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/config/zod-schema.session-maintenance-extensions.test.ts\nTests  13 passed (13)\n\n$ node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/commands/doctor/shared/legacy-config-migrations.runtime.session.test.ts\nTests  16 passed (16)\n```\n\n### Before fix: schema gate rejects zero values\n\n```\n$ echo '{\"session\":{\"maintenance\":{\"resetArchiveRetention\":\"0h\"}}}' > /tmp/cfg.json5\n$ OPENCLAW_CONFIG_PATH=/tmp/cfg.json5 pnpm --silent openclaw config validate --json\n{\n  \"valid\": false,\n  \"path\": \"/tmp/cfg.json5\",\n  \"issues\": [\n    {\n      \"path\": \"session.maintenance.resetArchiveRetention\",\n      \"message\": \"duration must be positive (use ms, s, m, h, d), e.g. 30d\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n### After fix: positive intervals still accepted\n\n```\n$ echo '{\"session\":{\"maintenance\":{\"resetArchiveRetention\":\"30d\"}}}' > /tmp/cfg.json5\n$ OPENCLAW_CONFIG_PATH=/tmp/cfg.json5 pnpm --silent openclaw config validate --json\n{\"valid\":true,\"path\":\"/tmp/cfg.json5\",\"warnings\":[]}\n```\n\n### After fix: `false` (documented disable) unaffected\n\n```\n$ echo '{\"session\":{\"maintenance\":{\"resetArchiveRetention\":false}}}' > /tmp/cfg.json5\n$ OPENCLAW_CONFIG_PATH=/tmp/cfg.json5 pnpm --silent openclaw config validate --json\n{\"valid\":true,\"path\":\"/tmp/cfg.json5\",\"warnings\":[]}\n```\n\n### Doctor detection → repair\n\nDoctor detects via parser-backed rule:\n\n```\nsession.maintenance.resetArchiveRetention is a zero duration — this\ncauses immediate deletion of all reset transcript archives. Run\n\"openclaw doctor --fix\" to remove it so the documented pruneAfter\ndefault applies.\n```\n\nDoctor repairs:\n\n```\nRemoved session.maintenance.resetArchiveRetention \"0h\" (zero duration);\ndocumented pruneAfter default applies.\n```\n\n### Unparseable values preserved for schema diagnostic\n\n`\"abc\"`, `\"\"` — not matched by doctor rule, not removed by migration. Schema diagnostic handles these.\n\n### Diff whitespace checks\n\n`git diff --check` passed.\n\n- **Not tested / proof gaps**: None.\n",
        "branch": "fix/resetArchiveRetention-zero-duration",
